      knife enemy is built from the thug''s branches with one more: Dodge, above
      Attack. When a strike is announced at it and its roll is under the enemy''s
      dodgeChance, the guard takes over whatever it was doing, its own swing included,
      and it steps aside. The dodge is committed: the guard does not stop it once
      it started. It prowls wider and quicker than a thug, by the arguments at the
      Prowl call site, and it never taunts. Its slash cannot be countered, which
      is on the attack asset and not in the tree.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"c401093e-fc6e-4efd-a322-1ba73c4b22a7","$type":"ArcaneOnyx.GraphCore.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4250.0,"yMin":-260.0,"xMax":-3950.0,"yMax":-110.0},"title":"Entered,
      never taken over","body":"The guard of Attack checks only at the door, on purpose:
      a swing that started plays to its end unless a branch above cuts it short.
      bt_verify reports it for that reason.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"90441dde-ccb6-4fb3-bc0c-49839d95b87d","$type":"ArcaneOnyx.GraphCore.StickyNote"},{"$ref":"12"},{"$ref":"17"},{"$ref":"21"},{"$ref":"25"},{"ScriptGraphVariable":{"returnType":"System.Object,
